00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
A federal judge kept Gemini's $5 million CFTC settlement in force after both sides asked to erase it. This is Prediction Markets Daily, episode 24. Journalism and education, never a bet. Judge Alvin Hellerstein issued that order on Thursday. CoinDesk reported the January 2025 agreement stays. Gemini has already paid the $5 million. The order still bars the exchange from misleading the commission or denying those findings in public. The agency told the court the case

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.940
should not have been brought.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.180
Hellerstein also threw out Gemini's claim that regulators forced the deal.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:41.660
The commission sued in 2023 over a 2017 review of a proposed Bitcoin futures contract.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.340
The company settled three weeks before trial without admitting or denying the allegations.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.580
His opinion says Gemini fought the case for about three years, then made a calculated choice

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.220
to settle shortly before trial.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.740
The block reported the court treated that settlement as voluntary.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:01.560
A later shift in policy, the court said, is not a reason to reopen the judgment.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:06.779
Kalshi has asked the U.S. Supreme Court for a month-long extension in its fight with

00:01:06.779 --> 00:01:07.299
the states.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.119
A litigator working with the company told Semaphore the firm is not rushing the justices

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:16.219
while rehearing petitions and forthcoming CFTC rules are still in the way.

00:01:16.879 --> 00:01:21.079
The company does agree the court eventually has to say whether states and tribes may treat

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:23.319
its sports event contracts as sports bets.

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:28.319
It's counsel is the lawyer who persuaded the justices to strike down President Trump's

00:01:28.319 --> 00:01:28.579
tariffs.

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:31.179
The third circuit has sided with CalShi.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:35.799
The sixth and ninth circuits have sided with the states, and Nevada told the ninth circuit

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:38.919
that a pending CFTC rule would not change that outcome.

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:44.519
Rob Lockwood of the American Gaming Association told Semaphore the timing looks like CalShi

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:46.939
has spooked about the court taking the case next year.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:52.659
He puts sports gambling at roughly 85% of the company's volume, which is his claim,

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:57.079
not a figure this show has checked. The litigator called the extension ordinary,

00:01:57.419 --> 00:02:02.719
needed because amicus briefs were due the same day, and noted Nevada sought similar extra time

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:09.559
in a related case. The justices have until January to choose cases for this term. CFTC chair Mike

00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:14.219
Selig told Semaphore earlier this year he would welcome a ruling because it would settle the matter.

