00:06:18.312 --> 00:06:23.392
Fees, the spread, and the cost of finding the other side are how a venue gets paid, and

00:06:23.392 --> 00:06:25.532
that is how it works on a yes or no book.

00:06:26.132 --> 00:06:29.192
Choice lets a user post a number from 0 to 100.

00:06:29.792 --> 00:06:32.992
60 means that user is putting the chance at 60%.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:38.352
The trade prints only when someone else takes the opposite side at that number, and unmatched

00:06:38.352 --> 00:06:40.312
orders can still be changed or pulled.

00:06:41.052 --> 00:06:46.792
Winners settle at 100, losers settle at 0, so a buyer at 60 has 40 points of gross

00:06:46.792 --> 00:06:50.432
room if that side wins and loses the whole 60 if it does not.

00:06:51.032 --> 00:06:52.832
That arithmetic is the contract.

00:06:53.352 --> 00:06:58.532
It does not crown 60 as the right chance, and it is not a free coin, because nothing clears

00:06:58.532 --> 00:06:59.832
without a counterparty.

00:06:59.832 --> 00:07:05.872
A 2007 paper in the Journal of Finance looked at every US corporate bond that traded more

00:07:05.872 --> 00:07:10.492
than 9 times from January 2003 through January 2005.

00:07:11.372 --> 00:07:13.692
Average trading costs fell as size rose.

00:07:14.312 --> 00:07:18.732
Higher rated bonds, newer bonds, and bonds near maturity were cheaper to trade.

00:07:19.292 --> 00:07:24.592
Costs were lower where prices were already public, and they fell again once Trace started publishing

00:07:24.592 --> 00:07:24.892
them.

00:07:25.452 --> 00:07:27.212
The path in that paper is simple.

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:33.212
Limit the sample to bonds with more than nine trades, measure cost against size, compare

00:07:33.212 --> 00:07:38.032
public prices with hidden ones, then watch the same bonds after trace turns on.

00:07:38.572 --> 00:07:41.892
Public traders, the paper finds, gain from that transparency.

00:07:42.552 --> 00:07:48.152
A 2020 paper in the same journal found the index credit default swap market still had two

00:07:48.152 --> 00:07:52.272
tiers after Dodd-Frank, even with a push toward all to all trading.

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:55.792
Client trades cost more than dealer to dealer trades.

00:07:55.792 --> 00:08:01.332
The paper says the gap comes from a larger, mostly permanent price impact, not from a

00:08:01.332 --> 00:08:03.152
separate story about a posted fee.

00:08:03.712 --> 00:08:08.152
Most inter-dealer flow was there for liquidity and used cheaper, slower protocols.

00:08:08.912 --> 00:08:10.452
Client trades were not anonymous.

00:08:11.112 --> 00:08:15.952
They almost always beat the executable inter-dealer quote of the moment, and dealers appeared

00:08:15.952 --> 00:08:19.152
to charge according to how hard they thought the trade would hit the price.

00:08:19.812 --> 00:08:24.752
The paper suggests that shape follows from client orders being rarer, larger, and differently

00:08:24.752 --> 00:08:31.632
informed. A 2023 paper in the Journal of Finance is the argument overscoring. Skip trading

00:08:31.632 --> 00:08:37.472
costs, and the Ho-Schwey and Zhang Key Factor model, plus the Berillas and Shanken Six Factor

00:08:37.472 --> 00:08:44.312
model, show high maximum squared sharp ratios and small alphas across 205 anomalies. Those

00:08:44.312 --> 00:08:49.832
models still do not span the frontier a trader can actually reach. Count the costs, and the

00:08:49.832 --> 00:08:55.032
Emma and French 5-factor model has a significantly higher squared sharp ratio than either one,

00:08:55.472 --> 00:08:58.132
with cash profitability versions doing better still.

00:08:58.752 --> 00:09:01.252
The paper's dispute is with the no-cost ranking.

00:09:01.812 --> 00:09:07.312
Tests that ignore costs lean toward models built on expensive factors, so a quote near 50

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:12.032
on a yes or no contract is still a price that has to find the other side, with settlement

00:09:12.032 --> 00:09:13.352
at 100 or zero.

00:09:13.892 --> 00:09:18.152
These papers say the cost of that crossing can be big enough to change which model looks

00:09:18.152 --> 00:09:18.392
right.

00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:22.152
They are not a reason to favor either side of a live contract.

